{"title":"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be complex numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37f81bbe609249e3204dffd3c3318416375a2c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|w| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac118165a79d78421fb8d5acb078b52be10f780f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z| = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1ad5014efe0a075b29e120193ecb3d31a3635c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\arg \\left(\\tfrac{w-z}{z}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"106\" height=\"22\" />. The maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec3c0401f657bf5e132dce9d0c0f06f66913e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2 \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f650522cfc3d38eaa6a9a999cc47058c18d72a97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. (Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d54e29433e3334fa39ccac861aba3bb8b9b1246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arg(w)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd8b0e8ad77cf7a53c0c66730a086546fc4d788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />, denotes the measure of the angle that the ray from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> makes with the positive real axis in the complex plane)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64cb5f7612f12822ae3164b32b68d685e3a1660a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\operatorname{cis}{(\\alpha)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c995b1c42a0ba93dc0b0abb542d01048c1c0462d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 10\\operatorname{cis}{(\\beta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b48875ecdb165d0b047b288e6ca9446cdccf35f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{w - z}{z} = \\dfrac{\\operatorname{cis}{(\\alpha)} - 10\\operatorname{cis}{(\\beta)}}{10\\operatorname{cis}{\\beta}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"220\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying both the numerator and denominator of this fraction by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65fae67a3977da083f796c9a11ec33cc87ac5564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{cis}{(-\\beta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> gives us:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a9758bfd6be01b8f13da02722ae74a4a7e43c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{w - z}{z} = \\dfrac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cis}{(\\alpha - \\beta)} - 1 = \\dfrac{1}{10}\\cos{(\\alpha - \\beta)} + \\dfrac{1}{10}i\\sin{(\\alpha - \\beta)} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"520\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4ab2f9357f67da1f9352644730edfed7e23471b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the imaginary part of the above expression divided by the real part. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/4356a96efd70cb56b58a04474f035984b7c23358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\alpha - \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. Then, we have that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b9e35cda2778ffadd61e9bf276fef1777e3c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\theta} = \\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x} - 10}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"152\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>We need to find a maximum of this expression, so we take the derivative:\n</p><p>Note (not from author): To take the derivative, we need to use the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quotient_rule\">Quotient Rule</a>. In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/5/ae583ded4a195aef0686afc14a0d9239c358bd5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x-10}\\right)=\\frac{\\cos x(\\cos x-10)-(-\\sin x)\\sin x}{(\\cos x-10)^2}=\\dfrac{1 - 10\\cos{x}}{(\\cos{x} - 10)^2}\\]\" width=\"545\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we see that the maximum occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab084b375c6a2e24d213338a694d1e247f032d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = \\dfrac{1}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77deb509b573f47a4a03a48f4bdb658bbc64d257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x} = \\pm\\dfrac{\\sqrt{99}}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c0d7400ca1d0a12be27147c485c7fca6bf1305f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\theta} = \\pm\\dfrac{\\sqrt{99}}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" />. Thus, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cc532cd4df8a85044d8e1b3068860b19feda2c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2{\\theta}$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14c121422d08e53b99f255c3c03453c316efb1f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{99}{99^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"28\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a741b33c2652e9b903f40a1420679d0dcdee06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0bf9b0ad760e285df6d5a9c81f47caf57be9c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 99 = \\boxed{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without the loss of generality, one can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> lie on the positive x axis and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/5424936d4ede28d53aef85a3c44f8ddf13a1cc3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$arg(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> is a measure of the angle if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f8ec8f66f0d87a9d6c9955ff542c93b3a81c9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be3b5fc3ced7a8e84cb26e8f93cf7023289514b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$arg(\\dfrac{w-z}{z})=arg(w-z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"200\" height=\"33\" /> and we can see that the question is equivalent to having a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e220396bf8f6704ea4a5f1745cc64ce339090b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/276f8f2cb09be71f3f269b7ae229ca73fa6ad205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA =10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4e71e9c0786b12fb9b4b5c67364147ed6e402f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd405d5f60fa5c4acac707cf26758bf7b908456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB=t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> and trying to maximize the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678baa4f1af0dca41e2e5eb70b88f59a97a09970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOA$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd36693114ba3666531ab3ee1593e6ac2cf460f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair O = (0,0); pair A = (100,0); pair B = (80,30); pair D = (sqrt(850),sqrt(850)); draw(A--B--O--cycle); dotfactor = 3; dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(45)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,dir(45)); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,dir(135)); dot(&quot;$ \\theta$&quot;,O,(7,1.2));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;, ( A--B )); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,(O--A)); label(&quot;$t$&quot;,(O--B)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"105\" />\n</p><p>using the Law of Cosines we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57d4d72a1d834403fdd5303693a561ff139668f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2=10^2+t^2-t*10*2\\cos\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"232\" height=\"16\" />\nrearranging:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/2150e2ba453141d9b72bc6f7b1519bc0da059f82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20t\\cos\\theta=t^2+99\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />\nsolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5a3b34841a0696e4e3afc4fda90bda98eead51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/5114321e05c80a4b7253db6465b09bb8e07f24bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{99}{20t}+\\frac{t}{20}=\\cos\\theta\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" />\nif we want to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we need to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5a3b34841a0696e4e3afc4fda90bda98eead51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />\n, using AM-GM inequality we get that the minimum value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476a53790f4c8325c2347238218d47e83d6269c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta= 2\\left(\\sqrt{\\dfrac{99}{20t}\\cdot\\dfrac{t}{20}}\\right)=2\\sqrt{\\dfrac{99}{400}}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{99}}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"328\" height=\"55\" />\nhence using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba4e3602e4df09e8711b3fd01b6ca619ea22495d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" />\nwe get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea929d45562f4df8779ff51227e7af2904ff197a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2\\theta=\\frac{1}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0bf9b0ad760e285df6d5a9c81f47caf57be9c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 99 = \\boxed{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: You can also realize that the max <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is when the line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b833a70e5b34465a7e1cc445231d569f21b81da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a18cc8ac8a47cb98152b2e45be021c0b8b7cf9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w-z}{z}=\\frac{w}{z}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"121\" height=\"33\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12e2a79d4b188093f9533a132d845d909879b146.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|\\frac{w}{z}\\right|=\\frac{1}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d8128e6f7b5a156d3c7d10d067d5613394f9f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{z}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" /> is a complex number on the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c00e9e2066800d5a55332a7fb456073bbce0a08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> and centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> on the complex plane. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> denote this circle. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the points that represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d8128e6f7b5a156d3c7d10d067d5613394f9f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{z}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> respectively on the complex plane. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin. In order to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d38bc5d336cee894c3c8b242b51f4d2a17bdb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"21\" />, we need to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/236d65f80d8bb888e0b27c52693252548a07f869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AOC}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />. This angle is maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Using the Pythagorean Theorem, we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a44acecf8e0ac611b305e380fe3f36d48abac7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AO^2=1^2-\\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\right)^2=\\frac{99}{100}\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/7588bc6a7b2232ea4545f009a6e143c1ddd74c24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan^2(\\theta)=\\frac{AC^2}{AO^2}=\\frac{1/100}{99/100}=\\frac{1}{99}\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>And the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c446e8b36f04f5162b7de2c81bb56e79d54749b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+99=\\boxed{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef6c755c76bd14dc208804d6b006b485f5f37ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega = a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d53c5712578a3bb7060ce89b3dbbc5d96155b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = c+di$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />. Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b6594587ab1d63834bbdbf4ee8ef8292aa9113.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^2+b^2)(c^2+d^2) =(ac+bd)^2 + (ad-bc)^2 =  100\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"20\" /> Further, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/66164c4dd4131125ea3aa35be778db4bbce1c355.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta = \\dfrac{ac+bd - (c^2+d^2) + (-ad + bc)i}{100}\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"39\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72b2ecb9242a175e8cbcf5e2a0a8f8882c3efff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ac+bd = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />. Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae87615573e88b49afae6d4640808f900a38d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| \\leq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f9811851782676e96b81ac5a912f012bb26e655a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan^2{\\theta}= \\frac{(-ad+bc)^2}{(ac+bd-100)^2} = \\frac{100-x^2}{(100-x)^2}\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"44\" /> Taking the derivative and setting equal to zero (or via substitution and quadratic simplification), we obtain max occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Substituting back in gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e81dbbec8ea18e3147bb9910aa9c737b7b3140c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />, and an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c446e8b36f04f5162b7de2c81bb56e79d54749b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+99=\\boxed{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e88887e4aeb0d87e1758cafffab072ce158fa52c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega=e^{i\\alpha}, z=10e^{i\\beta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"21\" />. We have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\omega}{z}-1&amp;=\\frac{e^{i\\alpha}}{10e^{i\\beta}}-1\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{1}{10}e^{i(\\alpha-\\beta)}-1\\\\\n&amp;=\\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)-1\\right)+\\frac{1}{10}i\\sin{(\\alpha-\\beta)}\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0cf4096c3116a73b96cae82987c78a4a38a8da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\alpha-\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3230e11561a7290dc4774c65dcff5e3ccd03f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> evaluates to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a824f2d86216522d8db7155140179cc4ab983833.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\frac{1}{10}\\sin{x}}{\\frac{1}{10}\\cos{x}-1}=\\frac{\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x}-10}\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"47\" />\nWe introduce an elementary method to solve the bound of this expression. We set it equal a new variable:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1d695ab20f909cc33c3f5c5d72906456366fd8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x}-10}=k\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"37\" />\nWe are interested in the maximal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, continuing manipulating:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x}-10}&amp;=k\\\\\n\\sin{x}&amp;=k\\cdot\\cos{x}-10k\\\\\nk\\cdot\\cos{x}-\\sin{x}&amp;=10k\n\\end{align*}\nBy the angle-addition formula, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd55ddce9d89824bb9d2b2b5b76446c2f6266c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\phi=\\frac{1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />, and we note that\n\\begin{align*}\nk\\cdot\\cos{x}-\\sin{x}&amp;=\\sqrt{1+k^2}\\left(\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\\cos{x}-\\frac{1}{k}\\sin{x}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;=\\sqrt{1+k^2}\\Bigl(\\cos{x}\\cdot\\cos{\\phi}-\\sin{x}\\cdot\\sin{\\phi}\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;=\\sqrt{1+k^2}\\cos{(x+\\phi)}\n\\end{align*}\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc8dc0ee9333430b094e890c527815c1f9f1fd74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10k=\\sqrt{1+k^2}\\cos{(x+\\phi)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"23\" />. It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae61f787d75be400deedcad1d3c67305e6f2a1c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-1\\le\\frac{10k}{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}\\le 1\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"42\" />\nSolving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/4/b245d7d9ff21e0cf9e23b2f3188bb7ddcef4c5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{99}}\\le k \\le\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{99}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"149\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore, the maximal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3230e11561a7290dc4774c65dcff5e3ccd03f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> evaluates to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c5a01d669fe2c7f4e4cc0c6527072cb2fdd9716.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan^{2}\\theta=\\max{(\\lvert k\\rvert)}^2=\\frac{1}{99}\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"37\" />\nThe requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c446e8b36f04f5162b7de2c81bb56e79d54749b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+99=\\boxed{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: If you are unfamiliar with the method above, note that we can also obtain the bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b04cada33f0129aca6602da4689afa4c9a5bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\cdot \\cos x-\\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" /> by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a092e566aefa4b7789581d8c69ca20c16226b54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(k\\cdot \\cos x-\\sin x)^2\\le (k^2+1)(\\cos^2 x+\\sin^2 x)\\iff  -\\sqrt{k^2+1}\\le k\\cdot \\cos x-\\sin x\\le\\sqrt{k^2+1}.\\]\" width=\"669\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yakhEuPy6Sg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yakhEuPy6Sg</a>\n</p><p>~sugar_rush\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I\" title=\"2014 AIME I\">2014 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2014\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017094250\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.054 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 575/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18679/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.692      1 -total\n 71.55%   13.374      1 Template:AIME_box\n 27.27%    5.097      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12550:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017094250 and revision id 288801. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}